/* book: lead: A thyristor, or silicon controlled rectifier (SCR), is a four-layer p-n-p-n switch with anode, cathode and gate. With the anode negative it blocks whatever the gate does. With the anode positive it blocks until a small gate current turns it on; then it latches and needs no gate current. It turns off only when the circuit brings its current to zero. Two internal transistors that drive each other ex */
