/* book Worked example 2: Q: An SCR with latching current IL = 50 mA feeds a load of R = 20 Ω and L = 0.5 H from a 100 V DC supply. Find the minimum width of the gate pulse.
   1. After turn-on the current rises as i(t) = (V/R)(1 − e−Rt/L), with V/R = 100 ÷ 20 = 5 A and L/R = 0.5 ÷ 20 = 0.025 s.
   2. The gate must stay on until i reaches IL: 0.05 = 5 (1 − e−t/0.025), so e−t/0.025 = 0.99.
   3. t = −0.025 × ln 0.99 = 0.025 × 0.010 05 = 2.51 × 10−4 s.
   4. Check: i(251 µs) = 5 × (1 − 0.99) = 0.05 A = IL.
   Answer: The gate pulse must last at least about 251 µs; with a 10 µs pulse this SCR would turn off again when the pulse ends. */
