/* book exam traps: The gate cannot turn an SCR off. Removing the gate pulse after latching does nothing; turn-off needs the anode current below IH and reverse bias for long enough (commutation). | IL is larger than IH, not the other way round. Both are anode currents. | VBO (forward breakover, the device turns on) is not VBR (reverse breakdown, the device is damaged). | Drawing the SCR on in the third quadrant: the conduction branch is only in the first quadrant (VAK and IA positive). */
