/* book exam traps: VGT and IGT are the values the drive must at least supply, not maximum ratings. The maximum limits are PGM, PG(AV) and the peak gate voltage and current. | R triggering cannot fire beyond 90°; RC triggering is needed for nearly 0° to 180°. | In T = R C ln(1/(1 − η)), using log base 10 gives 0.432 ms instead of 0.994 ms; the formula needs the natural log. | A pulse transformer cannot pass a long pulse: its core saturates. Use a short pulse or a pulse train. */
